# AI agent workflow

```text
Understand task → read relevant rules → inspect existing code → reuse patterns
→ identify boundaries → plan smallest change → implement → tests
→ formatter/linter/typecheck → review git diff → architecture check → report
```

Never jump from a prompt to a large rewrite.

## Do not

- Touch unrelated files or drive-by refactors
- Replace libraries or add architecture without a documented gap
- Silently change public APIs, env vars, schemas, or provider behavior
- Hard-code languages, voices, or vendor SDKs into domain/application/API
- Implement the whole product when asked for one slice

## Search first

Reuse ports, enums, error types, cache key helpers, and tests. If a provider/adapter already exists, extend it.

## After a change

Run the narrowest tests. Summarize files changed, behavior, and any new Assumption/Impact/Alternatives/Recommendation. Leave the tree in a state another agent can continue.

